        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes When Buying a Treadmill Under $200</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most disappointment with cheap treadmills comes from one of these four.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting a running treadmill</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Every motorized treadmill under $200 is a walking pad or a 2-in-1 pad with a short belt. Photographs of runners and titles that say "running machine" do not change that. If you want to run regularly, save for a folding treadmill with a deck of 55 inches or more.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying an unknown brand to save $25</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Below $120 the listings are dominated by sellers with no track record, few verifiable figures and uncertain support. The saving disappears the first time something fails after the return window. Wait for an established brand's sale instead.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the walking speed cap</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Some 2-in-1s limit walking mode to 2.5 mph, which is a gentle stroll. If you want brisk walking at a desk, check the speed with the handle folded, not just the top speed with it raised.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping lubrication</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A dry belt makes a small motor work harder and is one of the commonest reasons cheap treadmills fail early. Buy a bottle of the lubricant the manual specifies with the machine, and set a reminder.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

